    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_9684dd26",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image displays a child pointing to their eyes with the text 'all animals are our friends!' overlaid. The visual juxtaposition of the child's gesture with the text, combined with the inclusion of a dog and a pig, appears to be a lighthearted or ironic commentary on the idea of universal friendship with animals. There is no evidence of toxicity, harmful content, or hateful intent. The meme does not target any specific group based on protected characteristics, nor does it contain abusive, cyberbullying, misogynous, or propagandistic elements. The intent is likely to convey a positive, inclusive message about animal companionship, using the child's innocent gesture to emphasize the sentiment. The overall intent is to promote a gentle, affectionate view of animals as friends, without any harmful or discriminatory undertones.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_e6ff68c2"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
