      "description": "The user is projected onto the child (VisualMaterial entity) who is visually positioned as the speaker of the message 'all animals are our friends!'. The child's gesture and expression are used to convey a sincere, innocent belief in the statement, making the child the visual embodiment of the speaker. This is a common meme trope where the child's innocence is leveraged to make the message seem more genuine or universally accepted. The user identifies with the child's perspective, projecting themselves as the one who holds this innocent, universal belief.",
